      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Culinary History: \r\nA 20th century dish first served at a restaurant
    called Moti Mahal in Delhi 1947, fleeting India\u2019s partition. It is believed
    to have been invented by using leftover tandoori chicken with a rich tomato,
    butter & cream sauce, transforming leftovers into a dish that is popular within
    and outside of India. This dish is unique in many ways, but it is also the center
    of an on going legal & court dispute over who deserves credit for its invention."
